{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>So Esav returned that day on his way.</b> Esav alone — and the four hundred men who went with him slipped away from him one by one. And where did the Holy One, blessed be He, exact payment from them? In the days of David, as is said: ״כִּי אִם אַרְבַּע מֵאוֹת אִישׁ נַעַר אֲשֶׁר רָכְבוּ עַל הַגְּמַלִּים״ (1 Samuel 30) (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:55.458173312Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}